WEBVTT

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:18.390
Inside the darkness

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:25.020
my love softly blossomed

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.230
like a flower for the first time

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.030
I'm sure you don't realize it

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:42.750
You held out your hand to me

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:48.750
and although I found no strength to take it

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.470
I want you to hold it out to me

00:00:55.090 --> 00:01:00.760
for just a while longer

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:08.520
That is my ray of light in the darkness

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.650
I don't want to know the future

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:21.830
of my love just yet

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.090
Koyomi

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.090
Stone

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.090
Calendar

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.090
Story

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.310
What? A stone?

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.150
Yeah, a stone.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.610
What about it?

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.610
Well...

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:57.360
I guess it could also be a stone statue.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.700
A stone statue?

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.870
I mean, it's not a stone statue, but...

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:08.870
I was just thinking that Oshino might want to
know about it since he collects stories like this.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.120
Stories like what?

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.130
Urban legends, gossip, idle rumors, and hearsay.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:18.800
I thought the Seven Wonders of the School would fit right in.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.130
Seven Wonders?

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.890
We don't have any stories of students meeting an untimely death inside the school.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.640
Um... What are we talking about here?

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.940
I'm sorry, Hanekawa.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.020
You left out one too many details.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.940
I totally lost track.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.690
Uh, like I said,

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.200
it's a ghost story about a stone.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.540
Now I see.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.710
It's hard to say one way or the other if this is a stone or a statue.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.960
Is this the stone you were referring to?

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.210
Yup.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:00.880
Oshino helped us a lot over spring break, right?

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:10.060
I figured we could tell him if something ghostly happened at our school.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.980
As a way to repay him.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.440
I see.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.980
The school doesn't really have a long history,

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.240
so we don't really have any ghost stories as of yet.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.240
There's just one thing that's been bugging me.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.660
This stone?

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.250
Or stone statue... Or something...

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.000
Yes, exactly.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.250
You know, it used to look different.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:44.180
I probed around the school grounds when I first came here.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.640
Why did you do that?

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.480
Wouldn't you want to know more about

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.270
the kind of place you'd be
spending the next three years?

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.360
So, basically what you're saying is that
two years ago when you looked around,

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.530
this flowerbed didn't have the stone in it, right?

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:03.030
No, no. The stone was here.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.280
So what's the problem?

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.030
I told you, it used to look different.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.540
The stone was here, but the shrine wasn't.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.920
The platform wasn't here either, nor the offerings.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.540
In the two intervening years,

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:20.670
someone propped the stone up like a statue

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.920
and began to worship it.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.930
There you have it.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:34.060
We figured you'd be interested in hearing it.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:36.690
Hanekawa wants to thank you for what you did for us.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.190
It's hard to call this a story about oddities,

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.610
but it is interesting.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.950
I'll write it down.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.200
So what do you say, Oshino?

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.660
Two years ago it was apparently just a stone.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:58.830
Now, two years later, it is the object of religious worship for an unknown section of the student body.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.960
Do you think it's an oddity or something similar?

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:07.220
Physical objects turning into oddities isn't so rare.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.220
Is it being worshipped because it's an oddity?

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.720
Did it become an oddity from the worship?

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.350
I can't decide.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.730
Is it worshipped because it's an oddity

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.110
or is it an oddity because it's worshipped?

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.730
No, no.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.780
The question isn't whether it's an oddity because it's being worshipped.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.950
It's whether it's being
worshipped because it's an oddity,

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.240
or whether it became an oddity
because it was being worshipped.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:39.330
Well, I admit the tenses aren't the same, but I don't really see a difference.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.340
In this case, perhaps.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:46.090
It's kind of hard to tell just from your narration.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:48.300
Can you draw a picture for me, Araragi?

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.180
I don't really have a talent for drawing.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.180
Perhaps you're surprised by that.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.810
A sketch is fine.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:58.560
All right.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.560
Black

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.320
So the shrine looks like this.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:10.740
To me, the altar just seemed like a place to put the offerings,

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:16.080
but when I looked at the shrine itself it seemed like it was clumsily imitating something.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.170
Maybe I saw something like it at a temple somewhere,

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.840
or some wayside statues.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.750
I don't know.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.630
I feel like I've seen its shape before.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:35.060
That's the kind of nugget of wisdom I need to know first.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:40.140
Did you save it for last to trump up your erudition?

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:47.900
No, it was just a vague feeling and only putting it on paper helped me get the words out.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.280
I don't really remember anything concrete.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.910
I kind of feel like I've seen it somewhere before...

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.660
That something central about it isn't new to me.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.170
Do you know what it is, Oshino?

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.290
No, can't say I do.

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.170
However...

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.430
However what?

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.010
Don't just stop.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:17.010
Tell me if you figured something out.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.690
You seem lively today, Araragi.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.650
Did something nice happen to you?

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.650
All right, Araragi.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:29.070
Tell the prez this.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:32.030
It should be enough that she can understand.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.320
You can ignore the ghost stories for the moment.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:39.540
Try looking into Naoetsu High School's curriculum.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:45.790
Studying is what students should really be doing.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.340
What's going on?

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:55.680
Oh, I was just unnecessarily anxious.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.510
Hanekawa, please try!

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.600
You should be able to explain this in a way that I can understand.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:03.600
Please try, huh?

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.600
Black

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:08.020
Think about the curriculum we have at this school.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.950
Remember how we could choose
between art classes in our first year?

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:18.370
I picked fine arts, but there was calligraphy and woodworking too, right?

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:25.120
When Oshino suggested we look at the curriculum, that was what he was hinting at.

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:26.750
You mean woodworking?

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.670
If I remember correctly,

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:33.260
the people in woodworking had to make a small house of wood.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:37.640
Basically, one of the little wooden houses got turned into the shrine we saw.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.060
Judging from how it looks, it was probably a failed attempt.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:46.190
This is what I think happened.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:51.190
<i>One of the students was making a little house in woodworking and it went awry.</i>

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:57.070
<i>But since he made it in class,
the teacher told him to take it home anyway.</i>

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:01.950
<i>Since he'd only throw it away at home anyway,</i>

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.580
<i>he decided to sneak it into the school's garbage.</i>

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.920
<i>On his way there he walked past the flowerbed.</i>

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.550
It makes sense.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.420
The trash is very close to the flowerbed.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.840
<i>He walks past and sees the stone.</i>

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:23.310
<i>He looks at it and figures, well,
this wouldn't look so bad with a stone inside.</i>

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:28.560
The stone doesn't look like a statue because of the shrine around it.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.070
The wooden junk looks like a shrine because there's a stone in it.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.070
Both stop failing as their own objects.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.780
The other way around.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.070
It's the other way around.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:42.450
It's still a pretty childish thing.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:46.580
The student probably went home
after he saw his failure transformed

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:52.090
from something bound for the trash into a little shrine, a house, basically.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:57.340
And so produced a stone statue that seemed like it was the object of worship.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:02.890
And now I can relax.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:04.970
Thanks, Araragi.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.350
Why would you thank me?

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:13.150
You told Oshino that the shrine reminded you of something.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.320
I bet that was when he realized it too.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.200
It isn't imitating something that you saw.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:23.450
You once made the same thing in class, right?

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:29.960
I bet you took woodworking instead of fine arts.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.420
Yeah. Right.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.210
You're right.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:39.220
Case closed, then.

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.050
Black

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:45.310
Hey, don't run in the hallway!

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:50.310
<i>And now for the epilogue, or rather, the punch line.</i>

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:51.060
Black

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:58.570
<i>Obviously it was I who made this in woodworking two years ago,</i>

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:03.570
<i>didn't take it home with me, but left it in the flowerbed.</i>

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.330
<i>I understood the reason for Oshino's odd smile.</i>

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.830
<i>I'm sure he was desperately suppressing his laughter.</i>

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.830
<i>Is it being worshipped because it's an oddity?</i>

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.250
<i>Did it become an oddity from being worshipped?</i>

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:18.010
<i>Those were Oshino's words.</i>

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:23.050
<i>They were cheap sweets, but this stone came a long way.</i>

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:25.010
<i>There is no disputing that,</i>

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:31.230
<i>and perhaps my thoughtless actions turned this stone into an oddity.</i>

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:36.190
<i>Perhaps it turned from a normal stone into the stone statue I needed,</i>

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.530
<i>and from there into an abnormal oddity.</i>

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.150
<i>The normal becomes the abnormal.</i>

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.320
<i>Perhaps that is what happened.</i>

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:49.410
<i>In light of that, going to school without direction can have real consequences.</i>

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:55.710
<i>I decided to go back to the classroom and ask Hanekawa</i>

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:00.380
<i>whether being unable to appreciate normality meant that I was like stones and wood.</i>

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:08.310
This stone...

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.890
is just concrete.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:38.130
I kick a stone away to get rid of my worries,

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:43.760
I'm downplaying the flutter I feel this April.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:49.260
We were happy children full of curiosity,

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.270
I was the one who pushed you forward,

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:55.230
from that day onward.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:13:00.690
Let's escape our confines

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:06.490
and take our time along the way

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:13.910
Let's ride our bikes to far away

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:19.540
carrying our hopes and dreams in the basket

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:24.970
Is the future we heard so many rumors about,

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.550
a nice place to be?

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:30.050
Even if we ask our extending shadows about it,

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:32.770
we'll still be none the wiser

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:35.560
we'll still be none the wiser

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.940
we'll still be none the wiser
